.Sh NAME
.Nm udpspeeder-simd
.Nd a UDP tunnel that makes a high-latency lossy link usable with Reed-Solomon redundancy
.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm udpspeeder-simd
.Fl c
.Fl l Ar local_ip:local_port
.Fl r Ar server_ip:server_port
.Op Ar options
.Nm udpspeeder-simd
.Fl s
.Fl l Ar server_listen_ip:server_port
.Fl r Ar remote_ip:remote_port
.Op Ar options
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A tunnel for high-latency, lossy links: it sends Reed-Solomon redundancy
so the far end can rebuild dropped packets. Used alone it improves UDP
flows; stacked under a UDP VPN (WireGuard, OpenVPN) it improves every
protocol the VPN carries.
.Pp
This is a fork of wangyu-'s UDPspeeder; the FEC design and the tunnel
are his, and the fork adds SIMD kernels, a DNS-following endpoint,
socket marks, and measurements.
.Pp
The socket marks options are validated: a mark the host cannot honor
is refused at startup.
.Pp
This build identifies itself as
.Sy v1.3.0 .
.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Ss common options, must be same on both sides
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl k , Fl Fl key Ar string
key for simple xor encryption. if not set, xor is disabled
.El
.Ss main options
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl f , Fl Fl fec
x:y             forward error correction, send y redundant packets for every x packets
.It Fl Fl timeout Ar number
how long could a packet be held in queue before doing fec, unit: ms, default: 8ms
.It Fl Fl report Ar number
turn on send/recv report, and set a period for reporting, unit: s
.El
.Ss advanced options
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl Fl mode Ar number
fec-mode,available values: 0,1; mode 0(default) costs less bandwidth,no mtu problem. mode 1 usually introduces less latency, but you have to care about mtu.
.It Fl Fl mtu Ar number
mtu. for mode 0, the program will split packet to segment smaller than mtu value. for mode 1, no packet will be split, the program just check if the mtu is exceed. default value: 1250. you typically shouldn't change this value.
.It Fl j , Fl Fl jitter Ar number
simulated jitter. randomly delay first packet for 0~<number> ms, default value: 0. do not use if you dont know what it means.
.It Fl i , Fl Fl interval Ar number
scatter each fec group to a interval of <number> ms, to defend burst packet loss. default value: 0. do not use if you dont know what it means.
.It Fl f , Fl Fl fec
x1:y1,x2:y2,..  similar to -f/--fec above,fine-grained fec parameters,may help save bandwidth. example: "-f 1:3,2:4,10:6,20:10". check repo for details
.It Fl Fl random-drop Ar number
simulate packet loss, unit: 0.01%. default value: 0.
.It Fl Fl disable-obscure Ar number
disable obscure, to save a bit bandwidth and cpu
.It Fl Fl disable-checksum Ar number
disable checksum to save a bit bandwidth and cpu
.El
.Ss developer options
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl Fl fifo Ar string
use a fifo(named pipe) for sending commands to the running program, so that you can change fec encode parameters dynamically, check readme.md in repository for supported commands.
.It Fl j , Fl Fl jitter
jmin:jmax       similar to -j above, but create jitter randomly between jmin and jmax
.It Fl i , Fl Fl interval
imin:imax       similar to -i above, but scatter randomly between imin and imax
.It Fl q , Fl Fl queue-len Ar number
fec queue len, only for mode 0, fec will be performed immediately after queue is full. default value: 200. 
.It Fl Fl decode-buf Ar number
size of buffer of fec decoder,unit: packet, default: 2000
.It Fl Fl fwmark Ar number
firewall mark for the tunnel's sockets (Linux), 0x hex or decimal, 0=off
.It Fl Fl cookie Ar number
packet filter cookie for the tunnel's sockets (FreeBSD), 0x hex or decimal, 0=off
.It Fl Fl dscp Ar number
differentiated services code point for the tunnel's packets, 0-63, 0=off
.It Fl Fl delay-capacity Ar number
max number of delayed packets, 0 means unlimited, default: 0
.It Fl Fl disable-fec Ar number
completely disable fec, turn the program into a normal udp tunnel
.It Fl Fl sock-buf Ar number
buf size for socket, >=10 and <=10240, unit: kbyte, default: 1024
.It Fl Fl out-addr
ip:port         force all output packets of '-r' end to go through this address, port 0 for random port.
.It Fl Fl out-interface Ar string
force all output packets of '-r' end to go through this interface.
.El
.Ss log and help options
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl Fl log-level Ar number
0: never    1: fatal   2: error   3: warn  4: info (default)      5: debug   6: trace
.It Fl Fl log-position
enable file name, function name, line number in log
.It Fl Fl disable-color
disable log color
.It Fl h , Fl Fl help
print this help message
.El
.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Run a server for a UDP service on port 7777 and a client at
localhost:3333, with redundancy of 10 packets per 20:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
udpspeeder-simd -s -l0.0.0.0:4096 -r127.0.0.1:7777 -f20:10 -k passwd
udpspeeder-simd -c -l127.0.0.1:3333 -r44.55.66.77:4096 -f20:10 -k passwd
.Ed
